From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: saiththerobo <the.tom.sharp@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:43:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rtc: s5m: wait for the S2MPG10's read update before reading
 the time

On the Pixel 6 Pro (S2MPG10, through ACPM), reading the RTC returned a
stale time now and then: of 20 reads half a second apart, three were 1 s
behind the system clock and one 5 s, and an alarm set 60 s ahead with
rtcwake landed 31 s late. rtcwake sets its alarm relative to that read,
so the alarm fired early in one suspend and not at all in another,
leaving the phone asleep for 558 s instead of 20.

The S2MPG10 copies its counters into the time registers on a rising edge
of RUDR, and the copy takes time. The driver only sets the bit, which
writes nothing while it still reads 1, and reads the registers at once.
Do what Google's s2mpg10 driver does (s2m_rtc_update()): clear RUDR,
wait 50 us, set it, and wait 1 ms before the read.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: saiththerobo <the.tom.sharp@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/rtc/rtc-s5m.c | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/rtc/rtc-s5m.c b/drivers/rtc/rtc-s5m.c
index 27faa7f6a..c70384de6 100644
--- a/drivers/rtc/rtc-s5m.c
+++ b/drivers/rtc/rtc-s5m.c
@@ -343,14 +343,27 @@ static int s5m_rtc_read_time(struct device *dev, struct rtc_time *tm)
 	int ret;
 
 	if (info->regs->read_time_udr_mask) {
+		/*
+		 * The S2MPG10 copies the counters into the time registers on a
+		 * rising edge of RUDR, and the copy takes time: with the bit
+		 * only set (a no-op while it still reads 1) and the registers
+		 * read at once, a read could return a time seconds old, and
+		 * an alarm set from it fired early or not at all. Clear it
+		 * first and wait for the copy, as Google's s2mpg10 driver does.
+		 */
+		if (info->device_type == S2MPG10) {
+			ret = regmap_clear_bits(info->regmap, info->regs->udr_update,
+						info->regs->read_time_udr_mask);
+			if (ret)
+				goto udr_fail;
+			usleep_range(50, 100);
+		}
 		ret = regmap_set_bits(info->regmap, info->regs->udr_update,
 				      info->regs->read_time_udr_mask);
-		if (ret) {
-			dev_err(dev,
-				"Failed to prepare registers for time reading: %d\n",
-				ret);
-			return ret;
-		}
+		if (ret)
+			goto udr_fail;
+		if (info->device_type == S2MPG10)
+			usleep_range(1000, 1100);
 	}
 	ret = regmap_bulk_read(info->regmap, info->regs->time, data,
 			info->regs->regs_count);
@@ -374,6 +387,10 @@ static int s5m_rtc_read_time(struct device *dev, struct rtc_time *tm)
 	dev_dbg(dev, "%s: %ptR(%d)\n", __func__, tm, tm->tm_wday);
 
 	return 0;
+
+udr_fail:
+	dev_err(dev, "Failed to prepare registers for time reading: %d\n", ret);
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static int s5m_rtc_set_time(struct device *dev, struct rtc_time *tm)
